# Split SPM Architecture

This branch packages three independently built dynamic XCFramework modules. Preserve this separation.

- `VLPlayerLib.xcframework` contains shared player code.
- `BitmovinLib.xcframework` contains Bitmovin-specific integrations and extensions.
- `MuxLib.xcframework` contains Mux-specific integrations.
- All three XCFrameworks contain iOS, iOS Simulator, tvOS, and tvOS Simulator slices.
- Minimum supported platforms are iOS 16 and tvOS 16.

`Package.swift` must keep these products and target relationships:

- Product `VLPlayerLib` exposes `VLPlayerLibWrapper` and binary target `VLPlayerLib`.
- Product `BitmovinLib` exposes `BitmovinLibLinkage`.
- `BitmovinLibLinkage` depends on binary target `BitmovinLib`, `BitmovinPlayer`, and `BitmovinPlayerCore`.
- Product `MuxLib` exposes `MuxLibLinkage`.
- `MuxLibLinkage` depends on binary target `MuxLib`, `MUXSDKStats`, and `MuxCore`.
- `VLPlayerLibWrapper` depends on core VLPlayer dependencies only. Do not add Bitmovin or Mux dependencies to it.
- Google Cast, Amazon IVS, VisualEffectView, and iOS IMA remain iOS-only.
- tvOS IMA remains tvOS-only.

Keep `Sources/BitmovinLibTarget/BitmovinLibLinkage.swift` and `Sources/MuxLibTarget/MuxLibLinkage.swift`. Their imports force required binary modules and transitive frameworks to link.

Do not edit generated files inside any `.xcframework`. Source changes require rebuilding and replacing the complete XCFramework from its source project.

After package changes, run `swift package dump-package`, resolve dependencies, then build `VLPlayerLib`, `BitmovinLib`, and `MuxLib` for both iOS Simulator and tvOS Simulator.
